  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it, so I haven't seen a render. The particle behavior is the main uncertainty.\n\n- **Crystals:** There are seven custom crystals, built with `geometry.define` and merged into one mesh. Each has 5–7 sides, its own height, taper and tilt, and a pointed top. Every face has its own unshared vertices, a face normal for flat shading, and a separate vertex colour. The tip triangles are lighter than the side faces.\n- **Rotation:** The merged mesh turns slowly about Y, set per frame from `f.time`. It sits on a dark metallic cylinder pedestal with a rim disc.\n- **Sparks:** Two additive-blend particle emitters produce them. One is a disc around the cluster and the other a cone from its centre. Gravity is 0 and there is a little wind and noise. I didn't confirm which direction the engine emits from a disc shape, so the sparks may not rise as intended.\n- **Look:** The background is near-black (`#05060c`) with a dim neutral environment and a faint hemisphere light. There are two strong directional rim lights from behind, one cyan and one magenta. Bloom and a vignette are added.\n- **Contract:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and one `requestAnimationFrame`. The engine runs the loop. Frames change over time through the rotation and the particles.\n\n",
